---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Popcorn Ceiling Removal in Kissimmee: Cost, Process & Alternatives"
  description="How to remove popcorn ceilings in Central Florida homes. Scraping, skim coating, asbestos testing, and modern ceiling alternatives."
  ogImage="/images/drywall.jpg"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/popcorn-ceiling-removal-kissimmee/#article",
        "headline": "Popcorn Ceiling Removal in Kissimmee: Cost, Process & Alternatives",
        "description": "How to remove popcorn ceilings in Kissimmee homes. Scraping, skim coating, asbestos testing.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/popcorn-ceiling-removal-kissimmee/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Popcorn Ceiling Removal",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/popcorn-ceiling-removal-kissimmee"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Popcorn Ceiling Removal</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">Popcorn Ceiling Removal in Kissimmee: Cost, Process & Alternatives</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        How to remove popcorn ceilings in Central Florida homes. Scraping, skim coating, asbestos testing, and modern alternatives.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            Popcorn ceilings (also called acoustic or textured ceilings) were standard in Florida homes built in the 1970s-1990s. They hide <a href="/services/drywall" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">drywall</a> imperfections and reduce sound, but they collect dust, yellow over time, and look dated. Removing popcorn texture in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida requires scraping, skim coating, and <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">painting</a>. If your home was built before 1980, asbestos testing is mandatory before removal.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Why Remove Popcorn Ceilings?</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Outdated look:</strong> Popcorn texture screams 1980s. Smooth or lightly textured ceilings look modern and clean.</li>
            <li><strong>Dust and dirt:</strong> The bumpy surface traps dust, cobwebs, and smoke residue. Hard to clean without damaging the texture.</li>
            <li><strong>Yellowing:</strong> Popcorn ceilings yellow over time from age, humidity, and smoke. Can't be painted over without showing through.</li>
            <li><strong>Resale value:</strong> Homes with smooth ceilings sell faster and appraise higher in Central Florida. Buyers see popcorn as a project.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Popcorn Ceiling Removal Cost</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Popcorn removal costs $1.50-$3.50 per square foot in Kissimmee and Orlando, depending on ceiling height, asbestos testing, and whether you skim coat or just scrape.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Cost Breakdown by Room Size</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small bedroom (10x12, 120 sq ft):</strong> $180-$420</li>
            <li><strong>Master bedroom (14x16, 224 sq ft):</strong> $335-$785</li>
            <li><strong>Living room (18x20, 360 sq ft):</strong> $540-$1,260</li>
            <li><strong>Whole house (1,500 sq ft ceiling area):</strong> $2,250-$5,250</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Higher ceilings (10+ feet), multiple light fixtures, or asbestos abatement push costs toward the high end.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Asbestos warning:</strong> Homes built before 1980 may have asbestos in popcorn texture. Federal law requires testing before removal. If asbestos is present, only licensed abatement contractors can remove it. Testing costs $50-$150 per sample. Asbestos abatement runs $5-$15 per square foot (much higher than standard removal).
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Popcorn Removal Process</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Asbestos Testing (If Built Before 1980)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We send a ceiling sample to a certified lab. Results take 3-7 days. If asbestos is present, we stop and recommend a licensed abatement contractor. If negative, we proceed with removal.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Room Prep</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Remove furniture or cover it with plastic sheeting</li>
            <li>Cover floors with drop cloths</li>
            <li>Tape off doorways to contain dust</li>
            <li>Turn off ceiling fans and remove light fixtures (or cover tightly)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Popcorn removal creates a LOT of dust and debris. We seal off the work area to keep it from spreading through the house.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Wetting & Scraping</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We spray the ceiling with water (or water + fabric softener mix) to soften the texture. Let it soak for 10-15 minutes. Then scrape with a wide drywall knife. The texture comes off in chunks. Dry texture is harder to scrape and creates more airborne dust.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Painted popcorn:</strong> If the ceiling was painted AFTER the popcorn was applied, water won't penetrate. We have to dry-scrape or sand, which takes 2-3x longer and costs more. Some painted popcorn ceilings are better covered with new drywall than scraped.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Skim Coating</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            After scraping, the drywall underneath usually has gouges, ridges, or uneven spots. We apply 1-2 thin coats of joint compound (skim coat) to create a smooth surface. Skim coating adds $0.50-$1.00 per square foot but makes a huge difference in final appearance.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Skip skim coating?</strong> Only if the drywall underneath is nearly perfect (rare). Without skim coating, imperfections show through paint, especially under recessed lighting.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">5. Sanding & Priming</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Sand the skim coat smooth (220-grit sandpaper). Wipe down dust. Prime the ceiling with a stain-blocking primer (kills yellowing and seals the new drywall compound). Let dry 4-6 hours.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">6. Painting</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Two coats of ceiling paint (flat or matte finish). We use white or match the existing ceiling color. Total dry time: 24 hours before moving furniture back.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What Drives Popcorn Removal Cost?</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Ceiling Height</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Standard 8-9 foot ceilings: normal pricing. 10+ foot ceilings: add 20-30% for scaffolding and extra labor time.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Painted vs. Unpainted Popcorn</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Unpainted popcorn scrapes off fast when wet. Painted popcorn resists water and requires dry scraping or sanding, which takes 2-3x longer. Some contractors charge double for painted popcorn.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. Skim Coating</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Adds $0.50-$1.00 per square foot. Necessary for smooth ceilings that look good under lights. Without it, drywall imperfections show through paint.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Asbestos Testing & Abatement</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Testing: $50-$150 per sample. If positive, asbestos abatement runs $5-$15/sq ft (we don't do abatement—requires special licensing).
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">5. Room Complexity</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Lots of recessed lights, ceiling fans, or intricate crown molding slows us down. Add 10-20% for complex rooms.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Alternatives to Popcorn Removal</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            If removal is too expensive or the ceiling is painted/asbestos, consider:
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Drywall Overlay (Cover-Up)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Screw new 1/4" or 1/2" drywall directly over the popcorn. No scraping, no dust. Costs $2.00-$3.50/sq ft (similar to removal + skim coat). Lowers ceiling height by 1/2 inch, so light fixtures and crown molding may need adjustment. Good for painted popcorn or asbestos ceilings.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Ceiling Planks or Tiles</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Install wood planks, PVC panels, or acoustic tiles over the popcorn. Modern farmhouse or industrial look. Costs $3-$10/sq ft depending on material. Conceals popcorn without removal, but lowers ceiling height 1-2 inches.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Skim Coat Over Popcorn (Not Recommended)</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Apply joint compound directly over the texture to flatten it. Possible, but the compound cracks over time as it settles into the bumps. We don't recommend this unless you're okay with touch-ups every few years.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">DIY vs. Hiring a Pro</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            DIY popcorn removal costs $50-$150 in materials (scrapers, plastic sheeting, joint compound, primer, paint). Sounds cheap, but:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Time:</strong> One room takes 8-12 hours (scraping, cleanup, skim coat, sanding, priming, painting). Whole house: 40-80 hours.</li>
            <li><strong>Mess:</strong> Dust gets everywhere. Without proper sealing, it spreads through vents and coats the entire house.</li>
            <li><strong>Asbestos risk:</strong> If you scrape pre-1980 popcorn without testing, you risk asbestos exposure (serious health hazard).</li>
            <li><strong>Finish quality:</strong> Skim coating and sanding require skill. Uneven ceilings show every imperfection under lights.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            For one small bedroom, DIY might work. For living rooms or whole-house projects, the time and mess aren't worth the $500-$1,500 savings.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How Long Does Popcorn Removal Take?</h2>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Single room:</strong> 1-2 days (scraping, skim coat, dry time, sanding, priming, painting)</li>
            <li><strong>Whole house (1,500 sq ft):</strong> 5-10 days depending on crew size and ceiling complexity</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Most of the time is dry time (skim coat and primer need 4-6 hours each). We can work on multiple rooms in rotation to speed up whole-house projects.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Popcorn ceiling removal in Kissimmee costs $1.50-$3.50/sq ft. Process: asbestos test (if pre-1980), scraping, skim coating, sanding, priming, painting. Alternatives include drywall overlay or ceiling planks. For homes built before 1980, always test for asbestos before removal. Hiring a pro saves 40-80 hours of messy work and ensures a smooth, professional finish.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 my-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide">Need Popcorn Ceiling Removal?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-6">
              Safe scraping, skim coating, and painting. Asbestos testing available. Free estimates in Kissimmee and Orlando.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-sans">
              <a href="/guides" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">← Back to All Guides</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Professional Drywall & Ceiling Work"
    description="Popcorn removal, skim coating, smooth modern ceilings."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
